===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|chickenpox}}, {{l|en|chicken-pox}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|chicken}} + {{m|en|pox}}, under the influence of earlier {{m|en|hen-pox}} and {{m|en|swinepox}}, which formed larger blisters.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɒks|s=3}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-chicken pox.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# {{lb|en|now|_|rare|disease}} The [[blister]]s [[form]]ed by the [[varicella zoster virus]] ([[VZV]]).
#: {{syn|en|chicken pock}}
# {{senseid|en|Q44727}}{{lb|en|disease}} The [[highly]] [[contagious]] [[airborne]] [[disease]] [[cause]]d by [[initial]] [[infection]] with [[varicella zoster virus]], [[typically]] [[causing]] a [[skin]] [[rash]] that [[form]]s [[small]] [[itchy]] [[blister]]s.
#: {{syn|en|varicella}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=May 7 2009|journal=New York Times|page=A12
|passage='''Chickenpox''' parties, at which children gather so they can all be infected by a child who has the pox, are often held by parents who distrust '''chickenpox''' vaccine or want their children to have the stronger immunity that surviving a full-blown infection affords.}}
# {{lb|en|inexact|sometimes|_|proscribed|disease}} [[any|Any]] [[disease]] [[causing]] [[similar]] [[symptom]]s.

